  "meta": {
    "name": "Word captions",
    "description": "Word-timed captions: speech-to-text word timings grouped into phrases, balanced on two lines, drawn in two caption DNAs with karaoke.",
    "creativeDirection": "Direction: captions as typography, not an afterthought. Scene one is a calm talking-head voice: clean white Rubik, a soft shadow, and the spoken word lighting up in warm yellow so the eye rides the voice. Scene two is the hype cut: heavy Anton capitals with a thick outline, each word popping in pink as it is said, and the closing exclamation crowned larger as the one payoff line. Asset-free ink backgrounds keep the focus on the type. Review: no phrase exceeds two lines, no line ends on an article or preposition, the highlight never runs ahead of the word timing, and the crown is the only enlarged line."
  },
